# Copy to .env to change how the client behaves. Vite inlines VITE_* at build
# time, so this is read when `npm run build` runs, not when the page loads.
#
# The Vercel deployment does not need this set by hand. There is no
# client/vercel.json: the root vercel.json deploys api/ as functions alongside
# the built client, so the live console talks to /api/* and this stays unset.
# Setting it to 1 is the deliberate fallback for a static-only deploy. Do not
# also add it under Settings -> Environment Variables — two sources for one
# build-time value is a conflict waiting to be debugged from the wrong side.

# Set to 1 for the static, read-only dashboard: it reads client/public/data/runs.json
# instead of the API on :4000, and drops the trigger, approve, reject, delete and
# credential controls, none of which can work against a static site.
#
# Leave it unset locally. `npm run dev` proxies /api and /media to the Express
# server, which is what the full console talks to.
VITE_READ_ONLY=
